    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmisc\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\n**Hello o/**\r\n\r\nStarting with https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/commit/d1d950c00eb247cdedf6e03f7c58e305b8fc7b72, mini.nvim now introduce synchronization between neovim background and the terminal. I propose that we follow through by introducing synchronization for system-wide dark mode preferences:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5ea633be-e732-4a23-a323-12e6f9d15c4b\r\n\r\n# \r\n\r\nIn general, each system offers a way to query its dark mode preference:\r\n\r\n**Linux:**\r\n- Using `org.freedesktop.appearance.color-scheme`, which is managed by [xdg-desktop-portal](https://github.com/flatpak/xdg-desktop-portal/blob/main/data/org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Settings.xml#L34).\r\n\r\n**Windows:**\r\n- Using `reg.exe` to query `HKCU\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Themes\\Personalize`\r\n\r\n**MacOS:**\r\n- Using `defaults read -g AppleInterfaceStyle`\r\n\r\n### Example:\r\n\r\n> [!IMPORTANT]  \r\n> For the sake of this example, we are continuously polling org.freedesktop.appearance; implementations should consider using interrupts instead.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal timer = vim.fn.timer_start(\r\n  2000,\r\n  function()\r\n    vim.fn.jobstart(\r\n      table.concat(\r\n        {\r\n          \"dbus-send --session --print-reply=literal --reply-timeout=1000\",\r\n          \"--dest=org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop\",\r\n          \"/org/freedesktop/portal/desktop\",\r\n          \"org.freedesktop.portal.Settings.Read\",\r\n          \"string:'org.freedesktop.appearance'\",\r\n          \"string:'color-scheme'\",\r\n        },\r\n        \" \"\r\n      ),\r\n      {\r\n        stdout_buffered = true,\r\n        on_stdout = function(_, res)\r\n          local color_scheme = string.match(res[1], \"uint32 1\") ~= nil and \"dark\" or \"light\"\r\n          if vim.o.background ~= color_scheme then\r\n            vim.o.background = color_scheme\r\n          end\r\n        end,\r\n      }\r\n    )\r\n  end,\r\n  { [\"repeat\"] = -1 }\r\n)\r\n```\r\n###### Thank to https://github.com/ormai/dotfiles/blob/0488ab3b4e0660ac7af3311852ccba01aa189302/.config/nvim/lua/auto_background.lua#L13\r\n\r\n### Bonus (randomhue)\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4c6b1627-d88e-4d83-8f89-355cfae8c25e",
