            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nAt the moment I don't really the idea for at least these reasons:\r\n- It depends on OS dependent tools, which 'mini.nvim' tries to avoid. Not only because \"dependency is bad\", but also due to implementation and maintenance complications.\r\n- Implementation indeed seems to be either constant rate polling or something more complex. Both options are not good.\r\n\r\nI'll give it some thought, but at the moment it doesn't look like a good fit for 'mini.nvim'.",
