        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "\r\n@echasnovski, I'm curious to hear your thoughts on supporting **only** the XDG Desktop Portal specification. Since it's a cross-DE standard, it seems like a better fit compared to relying on *\"OS-dependent tools.\"* We have [D-Bus Specification](https://dbus.freedesktop.org/doc/dbus-specification.html) to communicate with through a Unix socket (e.g., `unix:path=/run/user/1000/bus`).\r\n\r\n**Example implementation:**  \r\nhttps://github.com/daurnimator/ldbus\r\n\r\nI'm particularly interested in the following for `mini.hues`:  \r\n- `org.freedesktop.appearance accent-color`  \r\n- `org.freedesktop.appearance contrast`",
            "created_at": "2024-09-10T13:30:55Z",
